From: Frank Liberato <liberato@google.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:57:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] [Fullscreen] Assert WebContents alive across tab
 fullscreen exit

Ensure that FullscreenController::NotifyTabExclusiveAccessLost() and
FullscreenController::ExitFullscreenModeForTab() do not destroy the
exclusive-access WebContents reentrantly by capturing a
base::WeakPtr<WebContents> and asserting that it remains valid after tab
fullscreen exit notifications and UI updates complete.

Verification:
- Repro (Before): out/Linux/unit_tests --ozone-platform=headless --gtest_death_test_style=fast --gtest_filter="FullscreenControllerDeathTest.TabDestructionDuringExitFullscreenModeForTabChecks" -> Result: failed to die
- Fix (After): out/Linux/unit_tests --ozone-platform=headless --gtest_death_test_style=fast --gtest_filter="FullscreenControllerDeathTest.*" -> 2/2 passed
- Regression: out/Linux/unit_tests --ozone-platform=headless --gtest_filter="FullscreenControllerStateUnitTest.*" -> 49/49 passed

